three GCP regions--

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:19.396
US East, Asia East 1, and
Europe East 1 as well.

00:03:19.396 --> 00:03:22.020
I believe that eventually we're
going to have both AMD and GPU.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.180
But right now, in open
beta, we have NVIDIA GPUs

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.620
available that you can connect
to Google Compute Engine

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.310
instances.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.476
FRANCESC: So the cool thing
is that you can adapt up

00:03:31.476 --> 00:03:35.580
to eight GPUs in a
single custom VM, which

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.830
is pretty amazing, especially
if you're running things

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:41.490
like TensorFlow or basically
any other software that

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.290
is GPU-accelerated.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.390
If you add eight
GPUs, you're going

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.660
to see a huge, huge
increase in performance.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.042
So definitely worth trying.

00:03:50.042 --> 00:03:51.000
MARK: Yeah, definitely.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.580
Cloud GPUs are tightly
integrated with our machine

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.650
learning platform,
so you're going

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.287
to see some big
improvements there.

00:03:57.287 --> 00:03:58.995
FRANCESC: On top of
GCE, you also have it

00:03:58.995 --> 00:04:00.430
on Cloud Machine Learning.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.900
So again, all these things, like
TensorFlow specifically, they

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.690
benefit a lot from GPUs.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:09.150
So if you're already
running something

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.730
on GCU or Cloud Machine
Learning that you

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.351
